findings.body:
The redesign drops the "Delete comment" item from the overflow menu, along with `handleDeleteClick` and the `DropdownMenuSeparator` import. Nothing in the file sets `commentToDelete` anymore, so the `AlertDialog` at the bottom of the component can never open and `confirmDelete` / `useDeleteComment` never run.

The result is that moderators can hide and show comments but can no longer delete them, which is the core moderation action. Nothing in the repo tests this list (no test references `comment-list-row` or the delete dialog), so the regression would ship unnoticed.

::diff{file="apps/posts/src/views/comments/components/comments-list.tsx" lines="328-345"}

::callout{type="warning"}
The dialog markup at lines 366-384 and the state/handlers at lines 149-157 are still present. That is what makes this look intentional when it is not. Either restore the menu entry (for example, a destructive `DropdownMenuItem` that calls `setCommentToDelete(item)`, with a separator) or remove the dead dialog and hook together.

The post title used to link to `#/editor/post/{id}`. It now filters the list by post, and the only other route to the post is the public `View post` link in the overflow menu. Moderators lose the quick path into the editor from a comment, which may be intentional but is not mentioned in the PR description.

::code{file="apps/posts/src/views/comments/components/comments-list.tsx" lines="236-243"}

If this is intentional, it is worth calling out in the PR. If not, add an "Edit post" item to the overflow menu.

The table header now has two empty `TableHead` cells. The old Comment, Author, Post, and Date labels are gone, so assistive tech gets no column semantics for this data table. The sighted layout is also harder to scan at a glance.

::code{file="apps/posts/src/views/comments/components/comments-list.tsx" lines="166-169"}

If the header is only there to hold the grid, consider giving the table an accessible name or a visually hidden caption.

The thumbnail uses `hidden ... lg:block`, so it is invisible below lg. The image is still in the DOM, and browsers still fetch `display: none` images. Every virtualized row on a phone therefore downloads a full post image that is never shown. There is also no `loading="lazy"`, which matters once a few pages of comments are loaded.

::code{file="apps/posts/src/views/comments/components/comments-list.tsx" lines="351-357"}

Render the `<img>` only at lg+ (with a media query or a `useMediaQuery` check), or add `loading="lazy"` and `decoding="async"`.

Several class strings use `${cond && 'class'}`. When `cond` is false, the template produces the literal word `false` in the class attribute. This is harmless at runtime, but it is untidy and was copied into new code in this PR.

::code{file="apps/posts/src/views/comments/components/comments-list.tsx" lines="194-194"}

The same pattern appears in the avatar `opacity-40` class (line 200) and in `CommentContent` (line 112). Use `cond ? 'class' : ''` or `clsx` / `cn`.

The reports badge uses `text-yellow-600`. The code it replaces used `text-amber-600 dark:text-amber-500`. Without a dark variant, the warning color is less legible on dark backgrounds, and it is a different hue from the warning color used elsewhere in the admin.

::code{file="apps/posts/src/views/comments/components/comments-list.tsx" lines="307-307"}

Use the same `text-amber-600 dark:text-amber-500` pair as the removed report line.

`formatDate` builds an `Intl.DateTimeFormat` string and then rewrites it with `replace(/(\d+),(\s+\d{4})/, '$1$2')`. The regex is tied to the exact en-US output shape, and it only removes the first comma. The result is "Dec 17 2025, 10:30 AM", which is inconsistent with the `formatTimestamp` output next to it.

::diff{file="apps/posts/src/views/comments/components/comments-list.tsx" lines="60-71"}

If the goal is a specific look, build it from `formatToParts()` or compose the string explicitly, so the format does not depend on post-processing.

The mapper returns `feature_image` as `null` when a post has no image, which is how Ghost represents empty fields. The admin-x `Comment.post` type declares it as `feature_image?: string`, which does not allow `null`. The rendering code uses `&&` and so works, but the type is wrong, and the same file already models `html` as `string | null`.

::diff{file="apps/admin-x-framework/src/api/comments.ts" lines="28-28"}

Change it to `feature_image?: string | null` to match the runtime shape.
